==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*īsarną}}, probably from {{etyl|cel-pro|ang}} {{m|cel-pro|*īsarnom}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*h₁ésh₂r̥||blood}}. Cognates include {{etyl|osx|-}} {{m|osx|īsarn}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{m|nl|ijzer}}, {{etyl|goh|-}} {{m|goh|īsarn}} ({{etyl|de|-}} {{m|de|Eisen}}), {{etyl|non|-}} {{m|non|ísarn}}, {{m|non|járn}} ({{etyl|da|-}} {{m|da|jern}} or {{m|da|jærn}}, {{etyl|sv|-}} {{m|sv|järn}}), {{etyl|got|-}} {{m|got|𐌴𐌹𐍃𐌰𐍂𐌽}}, {{etyl|sga|-}} {{m|sga|īärn}} ({{etyl|ga|-}} {{m|ga|iarann}}, {{etyl|cy|-}} {{m|cy|haearn}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈiːzern/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|n|head=īsern|īsern}}

# the metal [[iron]]
# an instrument or tool made from iron, especially an iron [[sword]]
# an iron [[shackle]] or [[fetter]]

===Adjective===
{{ang-adj|head=īsern}}

# consisting or made of [[iron]]

